      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from Daily News (London) - Tuesday 12 September 1939",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003E\u0022Wiggled\u0022 tripe with shrimps\u003C/b\u003E -fresh or potted- is good. For this cook the tripe till tender, trimmed into small pieces, then prepare a white sauce with some of the flavoured stock mixed with the milk measure. Use 1oz. butter, 1oz. flour, half a pint of milk and tripe liquor mixed, to 1b. dressed tripe and a gill of picked shrimps. A squeeze of lemon juice and a pinch of mace assure flavour for the sauce.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Ccenter\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022wiggled-tripe-wiggletripe.jpg\u0022\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022wiggled-tripe-wiggletripe.jpg\u0022 width=\u0022450\u0022 height=\u0022auto\u0022 border=\u00220\u0022\u003E\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/center\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E"
